prompt.text:
Implement a complete TypeScript module exporting:

```ts
export interface WorkEntry {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  details: string;
  finished: boolean;
}

export class WorkLedger {
  constructor(entries?: readonly WorkEntry[]);
  all(): WorkEntry[];
  flip(id: string): boolean;
}
```

The default constructor creates an empty ledger. IDs and titles must be non-empty after trimming; details must be a string and `finished` a boolean. Duplicate IDs or malformed entries throw `TypeError`. Preserve accepted strings and original ordering.

The constructor must deep-copy each flat entry. `all` must return fresh entry objects. `flip` finds an entry by exact, case-sensitive ID, replaces it internally with a new entry whose `finished` value is inverted, and returns true. An unknown ID, including an empty string, leaves the ledger unchanged and returns false. Neither construction, inspection, nor flipping may mutate objects or arrays owned by the caller.

